{"nodes": [{"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "label": "Unified Contacts Specification", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Draft spec replacing channel-specific address books with one canonical contact system across WhatsApp, Telegram, email, calendars, and future channels; a small structured core for reliable routing plus open-ended recording of new channels, facts, and narrative context without schema migrations."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_execution_time_resolution", "label": "Execution-Time Resolution", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contact resolution happens in a separate contacts executable via shell command substitution ($(contacts resolve 'Name' --channel X)); the communication CLI receives only its native identifier and has no knowledge of contacts, keeping communication CLIs independent from the contacts implementation."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_channel_independence", "label": "Channel Independence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Communication skills accept only channel-native identifiers and never read contact files, resolve names, or hold ambiguity rules; contacts owns people, aliases, channel identities, and resolution, and never sends messages."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_notification_enrichment", "label": "Notification Enrichment (Reverse Resolution)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A shared enrichment layer, not the channel producer, reverse-resolves inbound sender identifiers via contacts identify, adding the stable person ID, display name, and a safe selector when known."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_reply_command_rendering", "label": "Reply Command Element Rendering", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "reply_command is executable guidance rendered as an XML element rather than an attribute because command substitution contains shell quotes that become noisy and easy to copy incorrectly inside an XML attribute; behavioral guidance stays in a separate reply_hint element."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_hybrid_storage", "label": "Hybrid YAML Front Matter + Markdown Storage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Front matter holds data required for identity and automation (id, name, aliases, channel_identities, custom, tags, relationships); Markdown holds flexible narrative context. Unknown channels, attributes, and custom fields round-trip without loss so adding a channel never requires a storage migration."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_stable_person_id", "label": "Stable Person ID", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The id in front matter is authoritative; filenames (readable slug + short ID) exist only for human navigation, so duplicate names and renames never define identity. Relationships and synchronization anchor on person IDs, not names."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_empty_identifier_rejection", "label": "Empty Identifier Rejection Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every recipient-taking communication CLI must reject an empty identifier because a failed command substitution must never turn into a send to a default or implicit recipient."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_ambiguity_fail_closed", "label": "Ambiguity Fails Closed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Names are never parsed as phone numbers, chat IDs, usernames, emails, or JIDs (preventing collisions like a contact named '112'); ambiguous names and identities fail with a nonzero exit and empty stdout rather than selecting the first match. Fuzzy matching exists only in contacts search, never during delivery."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_contacts_resolve_command", "label": "contacts resolve", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Designed for command substitution: on success stdout carries exactly one normalized identifier plus newline, diagnostics never appear on stdout, and failure exits nonzero with empty stdout. Selector types are explicit (person:<id> vs exact name/alias) so spelling never changes interpretation."}, {"id": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_contacts_identify_command", "label": "contacts identify", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reverse-resolves a channel identifier to a person, returning a safe selector only when the readable name uniquely selects the person; otherwise the notification builder falls back to the raw originating identifier."}], "edges": [{"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_skill_contacts_markdown_store", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_execution_time_resolution", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_channel_independence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_notification_enrichment", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_reply_command_rendering", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_hybrid_storage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_stable_person_id", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_unified_contacts_specification", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_ambiguity_fail_closed", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_execution_time_resolution", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_contacts_resolve_command", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_notification_enrichment", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_contacts_identify_command", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_empty_identifier_rejection", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_execution_time_resolution", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_ambiguity_fail_closed", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_contacts_resolve_command", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_reply_command_rendering", "target": "agent_skills_contacts_spec_execution_time_resolution", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent/skills/contacts/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "ag